Compile parallel-RDP's shader variants off the emulation thread on MoltenVK

parallel-RDP asks for each specialised shader variant with
VK_PIPELINE_CREATE_FAIL_ON_PIPELINE_COMPILE_REQUIRED_BIT ("only if already
compiled"), draws with its ubershader when the answer is no, and compiles the
variant on its pipeline worker thread. MoltenVK checks that flag only before
converting SPIR-V to a Metal library, and compiles the specialised Metal
function for the constants regardless (MVKShaderLibrary::getMTLFunction in
MoltenVK 1.4.2). Every variant is a specialisation, so every "non-blocking"
attempt compiled synchronously on the emulation thread: 50 to 200 ms stalls,
measured on device as frozen gameplay and audio in Ocarina of Time.

Granite already has the answer for a driver whose cache control cannot be
trusted (NVIDIA): broken_pipeline_cache_control, which makes the non-blocking
attempt return at once. Set for Metal emulation as well.

Applied at build time by Vendor/n64-ios/build.sh, after 0004.

diff --git a/mupen64plus-video-paraLLEl/parallel-rdp/vulkan/device.cpp b/mupen64plus-video-paraLLEl/parallel-rdp/vulkan/device.cpp
index b56bc2b..8841fd1 100644
--- a/mupen64plus-video-paraLLEl/parallel-rdp/vulkan/device.cpp
+++ b/mupen64plus-video-paraLLEl/parallel-rdp/vulkan/device.cpp
@@ -779,6 +779,15 @@ void Device::init_workarounds()
 	// TODO: Use VK_KHR_portability_subset to determine this.
 	workarounds.emulate_event_as_pipeline_barrier = true;
 	LOGW("Emulating events as pipeline barriers on Metal emulation.\n");
+	// MoltenVK honours VK_PIPELINE_CREATE_FAIL_ON_PIPELINE_COMPILE_REQUIRED_BIT
+	// only before converting SPIR-V to a Metal library; the specialised Metal
+	// function it compiles for each set of specialisation constants is compiled
+	// regardless (MVKShaderLibrary::getMTLFunction). parallel-RDP's variants
+	// are all specialisations, so the non-blocking attempt blocked the calling
+	// thread for the whole compile. Treated as the NVIDIA case below: the
+	// ubershader draws until the async worker has built the variant.
+	workarounds.broken_pipeline_cache_control = true;
+	LOGW("Disabling pipeline cache control on Metal emulation.\n");
 #else
 	if (gpu_props.vendorID == VENDOR_ID_ARM)
 	{
